  "summary": {
    "use_case": "Multi-feature AI-powered learning platform: RAG chat over uploaded documents (Qdrant), a hand-rolled multi-agent problem solver (Analysis/Solver/Verifier/Hint/AlternativeMethod agents), exam-clone generation from uploaded past exams, teach-back evaluation, deep research (web search + RAG), and a code execution sandbox \u2014 all backed by a single OpenRouter model gateway rather than per-feature model wiring.",
    "frameworks": [
      "nestjs",
      "express"
    ],
    "modalities": [
      "TEXT",
      "IMAGE"
    ],
    "modality_support": {
      "text": true,
      "image": true,
      "voice": false
    },
    "api_endpoints": [
      "/api/v1/auth/login",
      "/api/v1/auth/register",
      "/api/v1/code-sandbox/execute",
      "/api/v1/webhooks/stripe",
      "/api/v1/problem-solver/{id}/solve",
      "/api/v1/chat/conversations",
      "/api/v1/knowledge-bases/{id}/search",
      "/api/v1/exam-clones",
      "/api/v1/teach-back"
    ],
    "deployment_platforms": [
      "Docker Compose"
    ],
    "environments": [
      "docker"
    ],
    "node_counts": {
      "AGENT": 1,
      "MODEL": 1,
      "TOOL": 3,
      "DATASTORE": 5,
      "AUTH": 3,
      "API_ENDPOINT": 5,
      "CONTAINER_IMAGE": 2,
      "GITHUB_WORKFLOW": 1,
      "DEPLOYMENT": 1
    },
    "data_classification": [
      "PII"
    ],
    "classified_tables": [
      "users",
      "subscriptions"
    ],
    "encryption_at_rest_coverage": false,
    "env_files": [
      "backend/.env.example",
      ".env.docker"
    ],
    "env_var_keys": [
      "JWT_ACCESS_SECRET",
      "JWT_REFRESH_SECRET",
      "DATABASE_*",
      "REDIS_*",
      "QDRANT_*",
      "CLICKHOUSE_*",
      "OPENROUTER_API_KEY",
      "OPENAI_API_KEY",
      "STRIPE_SECRET_KEY",
      "STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET",
      "GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID",
      "APPLE_CLIENT_ID",
      "TAVILY_API_KEY",
      "SERPER_API_KEY",
      "CODE_SANDBOX_URL",
      "CODE_SANDBOX_API_KEY",
      "R2_*"
    ],
    "local_url": "http://localhost:3010/api/v1",
    "uses_streaming": true,
    "streaming_endpoints": [
      "problem-solver (:id/solve/stream)",
      "chat (socket.io gateway)",
      "code-sandbox (execute/stream)"
    ],
    "total_loc": 900
  },
  "relationship_graph_md": "```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  problem_solver --> agents[Analysis/Solver/Verifier/Hint/AlternativeMethod]\n  agents --> model_gateway[OpenRouter Gateway]\n  chat --> rag_tool[KB RAG Retrieval]\n  rag_tool --> qdrant\n  rag_tool --> model_gateway\n  research --> web_search_tool --> model_gateway\n  code_sandbox_endpoint --> code_sandbox_tool\n  jwt_auth -. protects .-> code_sandbox_endpoint\n  jwt_auth -. protects .-> problem_solver_endpoint\n  jwt_auth -. protects .-> chat_endpoint\n  problem_solver -. reads/writes .-> postgres\n  rag_tool -. reads/writes .-> postgres\n  jwt_auth -. session/cache .-> redis\n```\n\nUnlike the ChapterApps/Phlox targets, Studyield's AI orchestration is hand-rolled\napplication code (plain classes calling an OpenAI-SDK client), not a\nLangGraph/CrewAI/LangChain-framework graph \u2014 so framework-specific adapters\nwon't find its AGENT/TOOL surface; only generic AST heuristics (class\ninstantiation + call-site analysis) will. The single OpenRouter gateway also\nmeans one MODEL node legitimately backs many different underlying models\n(GPT, Claude, Gemini, DeepSeek) selected by a runtime string, not one node per\nprovider."
}
